    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47094" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">susceptĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		suscipio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a taking in hand</i>, <i>undertaking</i> (good prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae proficiscuntur a virtute, susceptione
					primā, non perfectione, recta sunt judicanda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 3, 9, 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laborum dolorumque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ac. 1, 6, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">causae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Mur.
					1, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rerum istarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					9, 3, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An acceptance</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fidelium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Luc. 6, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
